---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">SOFTWARE ENGINEER · KATHMANDU, NEPAL</span>
    <h1>I build software for <em>complex systems.</em></h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">
      I'm Dhiraj Phuyal, a Software Engineer at Cedar Gate Technologies. I work on
      healthcare software, cloud systems, data processing, and developer-facing tools.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="#work">View my work ↓</a>
      <a class="button" href="/about">More about me →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="work">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">SELECTED WORK</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Engineering with real constraints.</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          My work sits at the intersection of application engineering, cloud infrastructure,
          healthcare data, and systems that have to behave reliably in production.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="work-grid">
      <article class="project">
        <div>
          <span class="project-number">01 / CEDAR GATE</span>
          <h3>DeIdentifier</h3>
          <p>
            A healthcare data pseudonymization platform for processing EDI, CSV and Parquet
            files while keeping protected data out of the browser.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag">.NET 8</span><span class="tag">Blazor</span><span class="tag">AWS</span>
            <span class="tag">S3</span><span class="tag">SQS</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="eyebrow">HEALTHCARE · DATA PRIVACY</span>
      </article>

      <article class="project">
        <div>
          <span class="project-number">02 / CEDAR GATE</span>
          <h3>EDITracker</h3>
          <p>
            A serverless processing and monitoring workflow for healthcare EDI, connecting
            object storage, messaging, Lambda processing and downstream data systems.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag">AWS Lambda</span><span class="tag">S3</span><span class="tag">SNS/SQS</span>
            <span class="tag">Firehose</span><span class="tag">SQL Server</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="eyebrow">SERVERLESS · EDI</span>
      </article>

      <article class="project">
        <div>
          <span class="project-number">03 / PERSONAL</span>
          <h3>Gravity</h3>
          <p>
            An interpreted programming language in C#, built from the ideas in the Monkey
            interpreter book, with a lexer, Pratt parser, AST, closures and a REPL.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag">C#</span><span class="tag">Compiler Design</span><span class="tag">Parsing</span>
            <span class="tag">AST</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="eyebrow">LANGUAGE · SYSTEMS</span>
      </article>

      <article class="project">
        <div>
          <span class="project-number">04 / ENGINEERING</span>
          <h3>Observability</h3>
          <p>
            Building monitoring and reporting workflows around production data, with a focus
            on useful operational signals rather than dashboards for their own sake.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag">Power BI</span><span class="tag">AWS</span><span class="tag">SQL</span>
            <span class="tag">Monitoring</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="eyebrow">DATA · OPERATIONS</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">EXPERIENCE</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>From application code to infrastructure.</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          I enjoy understanding the whole path from a user's action to the systems that
          process it, store it, monitor it, and eventually make it useful.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-date">CURRENT · 2025—NOW</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Software Engineer</h3>
          <div class="role-company">Cedar Gate Technologies</div>
          <p>
            Designing and developing systems for US healthcare in compliance with HIPAA,
            working across .NET applications, cloud services, data processing and monitoring.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-date">EARLIER</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Associate Software Engineer</h3>
          <div class="role-company">Cedar Gate Technologies</div>
          <p>
            Growing from an engineering foundation into ownership of application features,
            cloud workflows, monitoring and production problem solving.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">TOOLBOX</span></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Tools are means. Understanding is the skill.</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="stack">
      <div class="stack-item">C# / .NET<span>APPLICATIONS</span></div>
      <div class="stack-item">ASP.NET Core<span>APIs · MICROSERVICES</span></div>
      <div class="stack-item">AWS<span>S3 · LAMBDA · API GATEWAY</span></div>
      <div class="stack-item">SQL<span>SQL SERVER · POSTGRESQL</span></div>
      <div class="stack-item">MongoDB<span>DATA</span></div>
      <div class="stack-item">Docker<span>CONTAINERS</span></div>
      <div class="stack-item">Blazor<span>WEB</span></div>
      <div class="stack-item">Testing<span>QUALITY</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="callout">
    <span class="eyebrow">NEXT CHAPTER</span>
    <div>
      <h2>Still learning.<br />Still building.</h2>
      <p>
        I'm interested in systems engineering, distributed systems, cloud architecture,
        programming languages, and the practical side of building software that lasts.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/about">About me →</a>
        <a class="button" href="mailto:hello@dhirajphuyal.com.np">Say hello ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
